Core result contract

Every validation check returns a list of CheckResult values:

CheckResult = {
    "check": str,
    "severity": "HARD" | "SOFT",
    "message": str,
    "frame_range": (start, end) | None,
}

Interpretation:

Empty result list = check passed.
HARD = blocking/critical failure.
SOFT = warning/non-blocking quality issue.

The orchestration rule is that an early HARD failure should short-circuit expensive later phases, especially video decoding.

CheckResult.passed was intentionally removed; both HARD and SOFT results represent failures/warnings, while an empty result means pass.

Validation phases
Phase 0 — Dataset setup

Planned/current responsibilities:

load_dataset_info(data_root) — read dataset metadata, especially FPS, feature shapes, state/action dimensions, camera keys.
resolve_episode_paths(data_root, ep_idx, camera_keys) — dynamically resolve parquet and per-camera video paths while tolerating v2/v3-like custom layouts.
compute_dataset_stats(...) — compute action percentile statistics and episode duration/length/path statistics used by later checks.
Phase 1 — Structural

Current design:

Metadata length check — HARD.
Frame index continuity — HARD.
Required columns — HARD.
State/action dimension consistency — HARD.
NaN/Inf — HARD.
Episode length — HARD.
Phase 2 — Video / Vision

Current design:

Video existence — HARD.
Video decodability — HARD.
Video frame count — HARD.
Resolution consistency — HARD.
Video timestamps — HARD.
Image quality — SOFT.
Frozen video — HARD.
Multiview synchronization — HARD.
Camera coverage — optional SOFT.
Phase 3 — Actions / Tokens

Current design:

Action range — HARD.
Action smoothness — SOFT.
Gripper transitions — SOFT.
State/action lag — SOFT.
Action alignment — HARD.
Token budget — HARD when configured.
Tokenizer roundtrip — SOFT.
Phase 4 — Episode quality

Current design:

Idle ratio — SOFT.
Boundary idle — SOFT.
Duration outlier — SOFT.
Path efficiency — SOFT.
Task instruction presence/basic validity — HARD.
Instruction/video match — SOFT when an external VLM is supplied.
Proprioceptive synchronization — HARD.

Success-flag validation is removed. The real dataset does not provide a success flag, so no success check should be reintroduced.

Phase 5 — Dataset quality

Planned/current optional checks:

Duplicate episodes.
Task balance.
Diversity.

Some of this layer is still intentionally incomplete until the required inputs/embedding pipeline are connected.

Phase 6 — Orchestration / reporting

The validator orchestrates Phases 1–4 for an episode, scores/classifies results, and can run dataset-level checks when enabled.

