The currently existing configs/default.yml is the source for existing defaults and should be cleaned later to remove the obsolete success section.

Non-negotiable design constraints
Preserve the existing validator engine architecture.
Do not duplicate check logic in the UI.
Dataset path must always be supplied dynamically at runtime.
Use info.json as the source for FPS, camera keys, feature shapes, and dimensions where available.
Camera count must never be hard-coded.
Extra undeclared camera files are not automatically expected.
Missing declared camera files are HARD.
Do not use None video paths in EpisodePaths.videos.
Success-flag validation is removed because the real dataset has no success flag.
Keep HARD/SOFT semantics exactly as defined above.
Preserve phase short-circuit behavior for expensive operations.
Save the fully resolved configuration for every UI-run validation.
Add tests alongside every new source module.
Use dummy assets in tests before relying on real dataset runs.
Do not rewrite unrelated modules merely to fit the UI.
Treat actual source files and tests as the implementation source of truth; conversation summaries are a navigation aid.
Immediate next implementation step

Do not start by building frontend screens directly.

First implement the UI-facing engine contract:

1. control_registry.py
2. application/schemas.py
3. application/service.py
4. corresponding tests

The immediate goal is to make the existing validator discoverable and configurable by a UI without changing the underlying check algorithms.

Then add the API layer, then the frontend.

Working rule for future development

Proceed module-by-module.

For each new source module:

src module
     ↓
matching test module
     ↓
unit tests
     ↓
integration test where applicable

Keep the current implementation intact unless a concrete failure or UI contract requires a targeted change.

